Choose the step of the discrete quantile search from the mean as well as
from the normal approximation, so the nmath target stops timing out in
qpois(), qbinom() and qnbinom().

q_DISCRETE_BODY() in src/nmath/qDiscrete_search.h starts the search at the
Cornish-Fisher approximation y and steps by 1 when y < 4096.  For extreme
p, y can be far below the quantile, even clamped to 0: qpois(p, lambda =
2.68e154, log.p = TRUE) with p just above -lambda starts at 0 with a
quantile near 1.9e150 (oss-fuzz testcase 5898528638173184), so it never
returns, and qnbinom(0.5, size = 0.1, mu = 1e12) does not either.  Use
fmax2(y, mu) for that test and the initial step.

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #545 (no Bugzilla report yet).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

